# HeliSim ignores.

# Byte code, regenerated by the interpreter.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The scratch that was swept out of the root on 2026-09-28: page image crops
# and per-page extraction dumps from the reference PDFs, the pre-scenery
# main.py, and the throwaway greps that went with them.  Kept on disk because
# the numbers in the physics modules can be traced back through it, but it is
# not part of the project - see attic/README.md.  The directory is ignored and
# its bulk stays that way; the tools inside it that a check is run with are
# re-included at the end of this file, where the reason is.
attic/

# The reference documents themselves: third party PDFs and their 83 scanned
# flight manual pages, 42 MB that nobody needs to clone.  The OCR text files
# that the physics quotes are NOT ignored - those are small and are the point.
reference/*.pdf
reference/fm_pages/

# main.py's key log: the last flight's keystrokes and telemetry, written beside
# main.py and overwritten by the next run.  main.py --no-log does not write one.
keylog.txt

# What the scripted pilot scribbles: the console transcripts, compile dumps,
# probe output and main.py excerpts that accumulated in the root while the
# thirteen _rt_ modules were being worked out - _rt_log.txt, _rt_demo_log.txt,
# _rt_handling.txt, _rt_axes.txt, _rt_autoro_probe.txt, _rt_autoro_entry.txt,
# _rt_autoro_hand.txt, _rt_pilot_hand.txt, _rt_outer.txt, _rt_tail.txt and
# _rt_engine.txt are written by those runs themselves, and sim_demo.txt is
# simulation.py's own demo.  The modules are NOT ignored - _rt_pilot.py,
# _rt_check.py, _rt_demo.py, _rt_probe.py, _rt_handling.py, _rt_axes.py,
# _rt_autoro_probe.py, _rt_autoro_entry.py, _rt_autoro_hand.py,
# _rt_pilot_hand.py, _rt_outer.py, _rt_tail.py, _rt_engine.py are the harness
# and are tracked; only what a run prints on its way through is not.
_m*.txt
_rt_*.txt
sim_demo.txt

# What the _tmp_ tools scribbled, and the one of them that is NOT ignored:
# _tmp_shadow.py is tracked, because the Done entries in TODO.md verify
# _rt_axes.py and _rt_handling.py with it and a check nobody can run is not one.
# The other six - the sweeps, probes and one-flight diagnostics the autorotation
# cushion and the manual's flare were read with - went to attic/ on 2026-10-21,
# which is already ignored, and what they wrote (_tmp_*.txt, _tmp_*.log - the
# console dumps a redirection leaves, which are UTF-16 on this box - and the
# log_*.txt a detached run leaves) is scratch wherever it lands.
#
# Three more joined them on 2026-10-22, all with the ninth harness module:
# _tmp_hand_probe.py, which flies one of a module's entry points inside a try,
# and _tmp_syntax.py, which parses one file with ast - and with them
# attic/_tmp_counts.py, the tool that reads every `(N lines)` claim in
# README.md, TODO.md and attic/README.md back off the files themselves and
# exits 1 when one of them has drifted, so a count can be gated on rather than
# trusted to whoever wrote it down last.
_tmp_*.py
!_tmp_shadow.py
_tmp_*.txt
_tmp_*.log
log_*.txt

# attic/, revisited on 2026-10-23.  Ignoring the directory was right for the 131
# text dumps, the 43 page crops and the pre-scenery main.py in it - but it also
# kept out `attic/_tmp_counts.py`, the tool that reads every `(N lines)` claim
# in README.md, TODO.md and attic/README.md back off the files themselves and
# exits 1 when one of them has drifted.  That is a check, and a check nobody can
# run is not one, the same reason `_tmp_shadow.py` above is tracked: so the
# directory, its README (the third document the tool reads claims out of) and
# the `.py` tools beside it are put back here, and the bulk stays ignored.
# `attic/*` matches a directory too, so git never descends into `attic/_imgs/`,
# and `attic/_head_main.py` - a 380 KB excerpt of main.py rather than a tool -
# is ignored again on the last line.  These lines come last because `_tmp_*.py`
# above matches at any depth and would otherwise take the ten `_tmp_` tools in
# here back out with it.
!attic/
attic/*
!attic/README.md
!attic/*.py
attic/_head_main.py
